          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Two Variables, One Line"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.852,
            0.071,
            0.881,
            0.087
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "97"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.115,
            0.884,
            0.2
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The slope of the line using points A and B is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 3 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and using B and D we get "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 6 } { 4 }   =   \\frac { 3 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . We may therefore conclude that the slope of the line remains the same and is independent of where we measure it on the line."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.212,
            0.401,
            0.236
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.252,
            0.853,
            0.292
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Consider the point on the line AB whose x-coordinate is 8. What is the y-coordinate of this point? Express this as an ordered pair."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.294,
            0.854,
            0.334
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. What is the x-coordinate of the point on the line AB whose y-coordinate is 6? Express this as an ordered pair."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.353,
            0.879,
            0.393
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "B (1, 2), and C (4, 5). Plot the points and find the slope of the line."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.271,
            0.4,
            0.729,
            0.667
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.271,
                0.4,
                0.729,
                0.667
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_12_image_7.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.456,
                0.672,
                0.544,
                0.691
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 13.9"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.709,
            0.881,
            0.749
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Take any two points, say B and C, and find the ratio of vertical step (rise) to the horizontal step (run)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.753,
            0.462,
            0.791
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hence, slope "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{\\mathrm{CP}}{\\mathrm{BP}} = \\frac{5 - 2}{4 - 1} = 1"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.797,
            0.882,
            0.837
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It may be verified that we will get the same slope by considering any two points."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.84,
            0.882,
            0.881
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 6:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Consider the line in Fig. 13.10 which passes through A (– 4, 5) and B (–1, 2). Find the slope of the line."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
